WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.800
By coding along with me in this intermediate Python workshop, you're going to learn how to use

00:04.800 --> 00:09.680
object-oriented programming to organize your code. You're going to learn how to diagnose

00:09.680 --> 00:14.880
problems in your Python programs by understanding exceptions and even writing your own.

00:15.760 --> 00:20.160
We're going to work with new features in Python 3 that make Python easier than ever,

00:20.160 --> 00:25.360
such as F strings. You're going to learn a little bit about generators, a Python feature that

00:25.360 --> 00:30.400
allows you to loop over large data sets in a memory efficient way. You're also going to learn

00:30.400 --> 00:36.000
about list comprehensions, dictionary comprehensions, and other advanced ways of looping Python.

00:36.720 --> 00:43.440
Lastly, for the final exercise, you're going to learn how to use an interactive API and build a

00:43.440 --> 00:50.000
web application efficiently using the Flask web framework to make a really cool site that let's

00:50.000 --> 00:57.120
us filter GitHub repositories for a particular language by their number of stars. Taking a peek at

00:57.120 --> 01:05.680
that final exercise, here we go. We can filter by languages, submit, and our little web app is going

01:05.680 --> 01:09.040
to hit the GitHub search API and come back with results.

